- content_for :title, "% Results Ranked #1 · API Runs & Details · Gumshoe"

.page-header
  %p.text-muted= link_to "← API Runs & Details", api_queries_path
  %h1 📈 % Results Ranked #1
  %p.text-muted Measures how often each brand appears as the #1 AI answer across every run of a report.

.panel
  .card-header
    %h3 What it does
  .card-body
    %p For every answer in a report run, each mention has a rank. This query counts how many times a brand appears at rank 1, then divides by the total number of answers to produce a percentage.
    %p Tracked across multiple runs, it shows brand visibility momentum over time — which brands are consistently top of mind for the AI, and how that's changing.

.panel{style: "margin-top: 1.5rem;"}
  .card-header
    %h3 API endpoint
  .card-body
    %p.text-muted{style: "font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.375rem;"} Fetch all runs for a report
    %code{style: "font-size: 0.8rem; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 4px; display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem;"} GET /reports/:id/runs
    %p.text-muted{style: "font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.375rem;"} Fetch raw data for a specific run
    %code{style: "font-size: 0.8rem; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 4px; display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem;"} GET /reports/:id/runs/:ordinal/raw
    %p{style: "font-size: 0.875rem; color: #374151;"} The raw response contains a nested structure: personas → questions → answers → mentions. Each mention has a <code>rank</code> field. Filter for rank == 1 and count per brand, divide by total answers.

.panel{style: "margin-top: 1.5rem;"}
  .card-header
    %h3 How to run it in this app
  .card-body
    %ol{style: "font-size: 0.875rem; color: #374151; padding-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 2;"}
      %li Go to #{link_to "My Reports", reports_path} and click a report
      %li Click #{link_to "View Chart", reports_path} on any report to see rank trends across all runs
      %li Or use #{link_to "Test API", root_path} — pick a report and select % Results Ranked #1

.panel{style: "margin-top: 1.5rem;"}
  .card-header
    %h3 Run it directly with curl
  .card-body
    %p.text-muted{style: "font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.375rem;"} Step 1 — fetch runs
    %code{style: "font-size: 0.8rem; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 4px; display: block; white-space: pre-wrap; margin-bottom: 1rem;"} curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" https://api.gumshoe.ai/reports/22110/runs
    %p.text-muted{style: "font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.375rem;"} Step 2 — fetch raw data for run 1
    %code{style: "font-size: 0.8rem; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 4px; display: block; white-space: pre-wrap; margin-bottom: 1rem;"} curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" https://api.gumshoe.ai/reports/22110/runs/1/raw
    %p.text-muted{style: "font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.375rem;"} Step 3 — compute % ranked #1
    %code{style: "font-size: 0.8rem; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 4px; display: block; white-space: pre-wrap;"}
      # For each answer, check mentions where rank == 1
      # brand_rank1_count / total_answers * 100 = % ranked #1
